<!--Post: 4774--><!--Time: 1106740305-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4774"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitagirl31<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitagirl31<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 3:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Last night Kake tv, revealed a possible new communitication from BTK, which is the cereal box Tom has mentioned, however on the post card, it is asking Kake Tv, to let him know if they or the WPD received communication #7. Well they haven&#39;t. Also the post card that was sent to Kake Tv, had a return address of S. Skillet and with the address of the otero murders.  <BR>Now they also stated that there is two unsolved murders that took place in the 80&#39;s in the rural area of where the cereal box was found. On top of the cereal box was a red brick. Now it was stated that one of the unsolved murders, the crime scene had a red brick thrown into the window. So maybe BTK is possibly trying to tell us something new? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4774-->
<!--Post: 4794--><!--Time: 1106754036-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4794"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 7:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Now that would be interesting, someone needs to give the media a heads up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4794-->
<!--Post: 4800--><!--Time: 1106756245-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4800"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One of the murders mentioned on kake news, happened in 1991. I think it was Dee Davis.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4800-->
<!--Post: 4801--><!--Time: 1106756581-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4801"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tucker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tucker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very intersting about the brick, makes you wonder just how many mureders BTK is responsible for, as I am sure he trying to tell everyone something with these small clues.  I also wonder when and this mysterious communication #7 will be located and if the Wichita police are going to keep all of the letters content secret or release all of the info to the public.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4801-->
<!--Post: 4816--><!--Time: 1106763785-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4816"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 10:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Okay.  The New Mellenium Letters are as follows: <BR> <BR>#8, January 26th, 2005 &#34;Cereal Box Letter&#34; ... cereal/serial killer ... s. killet .... is a similar form to serial killer. <BR> <BR>#7 is suppsedly not found.   <BR> <BR>#6 December 14th, 2004 &#34;Plastic Bag Letter&#34;&#40;reports indicate it was dropped off earlier than that.&#41; <BR> <BR>#5 October 26th, 2004 &#34;UPS Dropoff Letter&#34; <BR> <BR>#4 July 17th, 2004 &#34;Library Letter&#34; <BR> <BR>#3 May 5th, 2004 &#34;Multi-Page Letter&#34; <BR> <BR>#2 April 7th, 2004 &#34;Baby Photo Letter&#34; <BR> <BR>#1 March 19th, 2004 &#34;Vicki Wegerle&#39;s Letter&#34; <BR> <BR>Old Mellenium: <BR> <BR>Jan. 1988:  Supposed BTK letter to Mrs. Fager <BR> <BR>April 1979:  &#34;Anna William&#39;s Letter&#34; <BR> <BR>Feb. 10, 1978: &#34;Oh! Death to Nancy Letter&#34; <BR> <BR>Jan. 31, 1978: &#34;Curly Locks letter&#34; <BR> <BR>October 1974: &#34;The First Letter&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4816-->
<!--Post: 4821--><!--Time: 1106764831-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4821"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 10:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry.  #8 was yesterday, the 25th, not the 26th<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4821-->
<!--Post: 4823--><!--Time: 1106766191-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4823"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 11:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well this brings up four unsolved cases. <BR> <BR>Marine Hedge and Delores Davis both were murdered near this drop off location.  Both cases have similar pieces of evidence to other BTK victims.  Phone lines were cut just as in other cases. <BR>Pantyhose was involved in BOTH cases, and pantyhose was in the #6 letter.  Both were strangled. <BR> <BR>Delores Davis had a brick thrown through the window.  There is a brick in this letter. <BR> <BR>My conclusion is simple.  Both these cases were the work of the BTK, and I would not be surpised if this information is revealed soon. <BR> <BR>Also brought up is the location of Carol Mould.  Her house was also near here.  Most likely BTK was not refering to this murder, but I would like to bring up that Carol Moul&#39;s case has a bit of a similar M.O. as Barbara A. Smith&#39;s murder.  Fires were set off in both cases, but neither of the fires really ever took off.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4823-->
<!--Post: 4831--><!--Time: 1106768027-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4831"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lazysean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lazysean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 11:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Your #2 - The &#34;Baby Photo Letter&#34; has never been confirmed as BTK-related.  However there was also a June letter that was supposedly sent directly to the WPD, so there are still 7 official communications on the list and 1 missing one &#40;apparently sent 1/8/05&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4831-->
<!--Post: 4849--><!--Time: 1106771012-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4849"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 12:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One thing Verm_inve. I don&#39;t know the location of the cereal/brick dropoff, but can the brick be ruled out as being merely a weight to keep the box from blowing away and being lost in a strong gust of wind? Just asking. <BR> <BR><i>&#34;Phone lines were cut just as in other cases.&#34;</i> <BR>Good point to remember, Verm, as there are those who still believe BTK about a ringing phone being the only thing which saved the Vian&#39;s kids lives. Pretty hard for a phone to ring if the lines have been cut, eh? This is a huge point because folks want to link children into each BTK crime. Fact is only the Otero attack was children and I will not change my stance that BTK was <b>not</b> expecting Josephine of JoesphII to be in the house. No question about children being a big factor in the Vian attack but they were unharmed. The photo of the infant which was mailed in cannot be proved to be BTK related; even if it is, where is the great significance. Since the Fox murder, children haven&#39;t had anything to do with BTK&#39;s attacks. My opinion is that yes, even BTK, worm that he is, would have problems murdering more children &#40;and after 1/15/74, he didn&#39;t murder any more&#41; but frankly, I think the bigger reason is that BTK understands the additional outrage which Wichitans would have if he, BTK, killed any other children. As Dr. Kelleher has posited, this man is a pure sociopath but he&#39;s very controlled and knows what&#39;s what. I believe BTK knew it was in his best interest to never murder children again. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4849-->
<!--Post: 4852--><!--Time: 1106773260-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4852"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 1:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, <BR> <BR>The &#34;phone ringing interruption&#34; might just be a sick jab on BTK&#39;s part -- he may be chiding the police knowing full well that it could never have rung. <BR> <BR>By the way, if this phone DID ring -- do we even have any evidence of WHO was calling at the time? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4852-->
<!--Post: 4856--><!--Time: 1106777365-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4856"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 2:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I thought I had counted them wrong.  That June letter is correct, and the Baby Photo might not be anything.   <BR> <BR>Sorry about that:  Updated list <BR> <BR>#8, January 25th, 2005 &#34;Cereal Box Letter&#34; ... cereal/serial killer ... s. killet .... is a similar form to serial killer.  <BR> <BR>#7??? January 8th, 2005 This letter has not been found.  <BR> <BR>#6 December 14th, 2004 &#34;Plastic Bag Letter&#34;&#40;reports indicate it was dropped off earlier than that.&#41;  <BR> <BR>#5 October 26th, 2004 &#34;UPS Dropoff Letter&#34;  <BR> <BR>#4 July 17th, 2004 &#34;Library Letter&#34;  <BR> <BR>#3 June 17th, 2004: &#34;Letter to the Police&#34; <BR> <BR>#2 May 5th, 2004 &#34;Multi-Page Letter&#34;  <BR> <BR>#1.5??? April 7th, 2004 &#34;Baby Photo Letter&#34; Unconfirmed letter.  This has never been identified. <BR> <BR>#1 March 19th, 2004 &#34;Vicki Wegerle&#39;s Letter&#34;  <BR> <BR>Old Mellenium:  <BR> <BR>Jan. 1988: Supposed BTK letter to Mrs. Fager  <BR> <BR>April 1979: &#34;Anna William&#39;s Letter&#34;  <BR> <BR>Feb. 10, 1978: &#34;Oh! Death to Nancy Letter&#34;  <BR> <BR>Jan. 31, 1978: &#34;Curly Locks letter&#34;  <BR> <BR>October 1974: &#34;The First Letter&#34; <BR> <BR>George-  About the brick.  If that was true I would have expected a rock.  However you&#39;re right that it can&#39;t be ruled out as a mere paperweight.  It is the position of the box being so close to Delores Davis&#39;s murder scene that has led a connection between the two. <BR> <BR>And you&#39;re right about the children.  Ever since the Fox attack children had little to do with his mindset.   <BR> <BR>Cutting the phone lines seem to have two purposes.  One is that there is no way to call for help, and second would be that a ringing phone would intterupt his mindset, and BTK probably spends hours before each attack getting into a mindset that he doesn&#39;t want to be disturbed. <BR> <BR>Though I believe that Hedge and Davis are the work of the BTK, I think I jumped the gun there too quickly.  One can&#39;t rule out the idea that BTK does like to toy with us and had gathered the information about the two murders from online.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4856-->
<!--Post: 4860--><!--Time: 1106778616-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4860"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 2:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is probably not relevant - and I am not sure of its exact location - but outside of Valley Center &#40;don&#39;t know if it was the bridge DD was found under&#41; but there is a bridge &#40;small, plain, concrete&#41; that now replaces an historic bridge called Theorosa&#39;s Bridge.   <BR> <BR>By all accounts - the locals say it is haunted by either the baby, Theorosa, or her mother who flung the baby into the creek below.   <BR> <BR>Probably not the same bridge - but I wanted to share that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4860-->
<!--Post: 4874--><!--Time: 1106787007-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4874"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 4:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Regarding the brick holding down the box:  I think this fits btk perfectly.  For anyone who has not lived in that part of the country, the wind will definitely blow away anything not secutred.  The wind is not always terribly strong, but it almost NEVER stops!  btk is organized to the point of obsessive compulsive personality.  He would bring along a weight to hold down the box, not take the chance of finding one at the scene, and a brick is so much cleaner and neater than a mere rock.  Remember the Saturday Night Live character the Anal Retentive Chef?  &#34;To dispose of our refuse we place the refuse in a clean paper bag, folding the top over three times and held closed with a pice of tape centered over the fold&#34;. <BR>That&#39;s btk.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4874-->
<!--Post: 4884--><!--Time: 1106794139-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4884"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 6:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe BTK? chose Post Toasties because this year is the companies 108th birthday. Tom&#39;s birthday is 1/08. It&#39;s on the Post Toasties website.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
