<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4971"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tucker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tucker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wichitan....the brick representing the brick thrown through the backdoor was my exact my thought as well.  I think BTK is definetly responsible for more murders than we know of and he is giving the police clues to which unsolved murders were indeed him, as I am sure it must be torterous for him to not recieve the credit for his own work.  Yet because of his style, he just cannot come out and say, &#34;I killed him, her, him and her,&#34; he must do it in his very cryptic, mysterious pattern of doing things. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4971-->
<!--Post: 4996--><!--Time: 1106846678-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4996"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 9:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Right on, Victor! It&#39;s a losing battle, though. I mean, at least half of these posts are convinced that BTK did Hedge and Davis because a brick was holding down the cereal box. Scott B&#39;s severed hand theory is brilliant when compared to the beliefs about the brick. <BR> <BR>Tucker: BTK provided definite information about: The Oteros, Vian, Fox, Wegerle, and a letter to Williams. Detailed descriptions and drawings were provided which only the killer could have known. The brick is BTK&#39;s way of stirring up interest in two murders which BTK <i>knows</i> many think he <i>may</i> <BR>have committed. I&#39;ll consider Ms. Hedge and Ms. Davis definite BTK victims if and when BTK provides similar information to LE which he did with his other murders. There is NO proof BTK murdered Hedge or Davis. NONE. Don&#39;t make it easy on BTK and give him so much credit, eveyone. Or, if you want to find him guilty because of publically available information - information available for an eternity - about a brick, go right ahead. No wonder BTK&#39;s never been caught: people believe everything he says and/or make evil mountains out of innocent mole hills. -- And I&#39;m just as guilty of the same behavior at times, I admit. It is easy to get caught up in the heat of the moment but at the end of the day, think over how meaningless &#40;in terms of BTK murdering Hedge and Davis&#41; this is <i>at this time.</i> A brick being thrown through a window &#40;hardly BTK&#39;s style, but never mind that&#41; and female victims, one in her fifties and one in her sixties &#40;twice the age of BTK-preferred victims but never mind&#41;  and both victims being abducted &#40;something BTK has never done, but never mind&#41; just pale in comparison to a brick holding down a cereal box!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4996-->
<!--Post: 5020--><!--Time: 1106850365-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5020"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 10:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is a long shot, but hey might as well throw it out there: <BR> <BR>Post Toasties = Post toas ties = &#40;bed&#41;post toes ties.   <BR> <BR>From the complete Otero letters &#34;Joe: <BR>Position: Southwest bedroom, feet tie to the bed.&#34; <BR> <BR>So it could be relative. <BR> <BR>Also, phonetically it sounds like: <BR> <BR>Pose toes east.  I&#39;m really good at that game MAD GAB.  Hehehe.  Maybe BTK is likewise!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5020-->
<!--Post: 5031--><!--Time: 1106854533-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5031"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ashbalti<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ashbalti<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 11:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was reading an article regarding the last drop on the Eagle web site and it said something about hearing trains and cars riding over train tracks at the area the cereal box was dumped. I thought that was weird considering BTK&#39;s profile said he lived near train tracks. Maybe the drop place was near his residence as a child? Just a thought. Maybe a little far off? Just Thinking.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5031-->
<!--Post: 5032--><!--Time: 1106854631-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5032"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tucker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tucker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 11:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, I agree that a brick alone is not enough evidence to convict of the murders.  But why a brick?  Its not like you find many bricks laying roadside, so he obvioulsy consciously choose the brick for a reason.  BTK is not one to do something randomly and without purpose.  And who is to say that the man cannot kill an elderly woman, or abduct them, or throw a brick?  Is that what the experts say?  The same experts who have absolutely no clue as to who this man is or where he is?  No one, not me or you, can say if BTK is responsible for more murders, but I would be hesitant to say he is or isn&#39;t just because one murder did not mirror another one.  These women&#39;s phone lines were cut, and they were strangled...perhaps they were older cause BTK was older and may not have been able to handle the struggle of a twentysomethings woman.  He can change his patterns up a bit, and probably has before when killing.  Before yesterday BTK has never dropped a communique outside of Wichita, so does that mean this cereal box is a hoax?  I mean, he has never done that before, so it must not be BTK according to your thoughts.  You can have your opinion, but I think what makes BTK so elusive is that he can be all over the map...if he is so predictable and only does things one certain way, don&#39;t you think he would have been caught by now?  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5032-->
<!--Post: 5035--><!--Time: 1106854956-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5035"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 11:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1372046.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1372046.html</a> <BR> <BR>heres the news conference.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5035-->
<!--Post: 5051--><!--Time: 1106857827-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5051"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 12:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tucker wrote, <i>But why a brick</i>. <BR> <BR>BTK reads all same information we do and therefore knows that Hedge and Davis are very high on the &#34;possible&#34; list. He would have known this for some time. Sociopaths will take credit for murders committed by others. I never said Hedge and Davis <i>weren&#39;t</i> BTK victims, don&#39;t misquote me. I said that the box alone really didn&#39;t prove anything to me; the brick is, in my opinion, BTK&#39;s way of trying to hint at and take credit for two crimes he <b>maybe</b> didn&#39;t commit. You can also have your opinion. Earlier I saw a couple of posts which were already declaring Hedge and Davis definite BTK victims. But sure, speculate until the cows come home - that&#39;s why the board is here. <BR>As an FYI, phone lines being cut is a very common thing. Abduction of victims in their 50s and 60s isn&#39;t. We&#39;ll find out. It may or may not be BTK. I never said BTK&#39;s killings had to &#34;mirror&#34; each other. Don&#39;t misquote me. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5051-->
<!--Post: 5079--><!--Time: 1106863804-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5079"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 2:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, <BR>Is it possible that he likes killing women slightly older than he, so he progressively chose older women as he, too, aged? <BR>Also, speculation about Hedge and Davis was apparently rampant BEFORE the brick. I don&#39;t believe the brick is a &#34;clue&#34; to his possible involvement, but I do believe he killed Davis, based on the similarities.  <BR>Also, was the Fager letter confirmed as a communique from BTL? If so, that certainly suggests that he DOESN&#39;T intend to take credit for murders he didn&#39;t commit.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5079-->
<!--Post: 5086--><!--Time: 1106866609-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5086"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 2:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I remember you from the A&amp;E Board.  <BR> <BR><i>&#34;Is it possible that he likes killing women slightly older than he, so he progressively chose older women as he, too, aged?</i>  <BR>Anything&#39;s possible. Davis was killed in 1991, age 57. This puts her at age 52 in 1986, when BTK <BR>definitely killed Wegerle, age 28. Wegerle is a definite, Davis isn&#39;t. Big difference in age there. I speak of Fager elsehere. However, I don&#39;t understand this, <i>&#34;If so, that certainly suggests that he DOESN&#39;T intend to take credit for murders he didn&#39;t commit.&#34;</i> That&#39;s possible, but of course if he doesn&#39;t intend to take credit it&#39;s entirely counter-intuitive and counter-productive, as he&#39;ll have no proof he&#39;s killed anyone except his known kills. BTK is brighter than that. So you&#39;ve determined BTK killed Davis. Cool. That&#39;s an awfully bold statement, labeling a possible as definite because of a couple of paragraphs in a newspaper. Even I wouldn&#39;t be that careless. But that&#39;s what makes America great, we can disagree and still endeavor to capture this fiend.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5086-->
<!--Post: 5127--><!--Time: 1106887103-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5127"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe BTK, the cereal killer, was &#34;Posting a Toast&#34; to Tom&#39;s &#34;awesome birthday gift&#34; &#40;trip photo&#41;. Remember there was the beverage &#40;1895&#41; before the dry cereal &#40;1897&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5127-->
<!--Post: 5128--><!--Time: 1106887430-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5128"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve never been on the A&amp;E board. <BR>Good point about Wegerle. <BR>I guess you misunderstood my point about Fager, however: if BTL would go to the trouble to notify the police of a crime he wasn&#39;t responsible for, why would he use the same effort to take responsibility for other crimes he didn&#39;t commit? <BR> <BR>BTW, as you may re-read above, I did not write that I &#34;determined&#34; that he killed Davis. To determine his guilt would require solid evidence. I used the word &#34;believe&#34;, which--I&#39;m sure I don&#39;t need to explain--usually indicates an attitude unsupported by solid evidence. It was hardly a definitive statement.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5128-->
<!--Post: 5130--><!--Time: 1106890575-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5130"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 9:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe in God and am protective of my beliefs about anything. The words believe and beliefs are pretty potent in this context. That&#39;s a  disingenuous - I&#39;m sure I don&#39;t have to explain the definition of disingenuous - second half of your post.  <BR> <BR>But what of BTK? Apparently you also misunderstand and may re-read that what I mean is BTK is being handed the Hedge and Davis murders by many naive, histrionic people without BTK&#39;s actually having to prove them. I&#39;m sure he&#39;s thanking you for Davis right now. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
