<!--Post: 5133--><!--Time: 1106893067-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5133"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Clairevoient<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Clairevoient<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 10:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why did  B_ _T_ _ _K® choose a Post Toasties® box? <BR> <BR>Check out pleasedeleteme’s post in Messages to BTK part 3 from Wed. 1/26 @ 8:46am <BR> <BR>Post Toasties® <BR> <BR>Anagrams into: <BR> <BR>sPiTs at ote®os <BR> <BR>“There are several other funny word games to play with these letters &#40;even some nasty ones&#41;!” <BR> <BR>Just play with these leftovers for a minute to see for yourself  --  S P I T S A T  <BR> <BR>Imagine B_ _T_ _ _K®’s glee when he discovered this wordplay. <BR> <BR>Catchers solutions are far more clever and probably made someone very jealous! <BR> <BR>What a buzzkill for B_ _T_ _ _K®. <BR> <BR>Way to go Catcher. <BR> <BR>Now Zodiac – there was a puzzlemaster. He could eat a bowl of Alpha-Bits® and crap a better cryptogram than B_ _T_ _ _K®!   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
