<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5146"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 7:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Clairevoient, I hope to give him even more buzzkills in the future!  It&#39;s always interesting to see everyones interpretations, I hope we&#39;ll find out who was correct in the end.  Until then, lets keep the victim&#39;s close to our thoughts and hearts in the hope that we may end this horrible game.   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5146-->
<!--Post: 5221--><!--Time: 1106953736-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5221"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 3:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->LE needs to relese everything that they do not need to authenticate communication. For god&#39;s sake, what if there has been something locked away in an evidence room for decades that would have sparked something that would have identified BTK? <BR> <BR>I know LE monitors these posts. Think about it, there is NOTHING to lose. You can no longer afford to rely on the &#34;he&#39;ll slip up one of these days&#34; theory. He has not and will not! Put the letters/communication out for the public. Tell them what has been in these mysterious packages, everything.  <BR> <BR>America&#39;s Most Wanted has been the most successful tool in apprehending suspects/fugitives, why? Because someone, somewhere knows something that will break ANY case. Including BTK.  <BR> <BR>I understand, you don&#39;t want to give him too much publicity. Too Late!!! I understand you don&#39;t want a hysterical community. Too Late!!!  <BR> <BR>The best possible outcome of the current investigation is BTK dies and he never pays for his crimes. Is that what you want? <BR> <BR>Tom, sorry if this is in the wrong thread. I couldn&#39;t decide the appropriate place. If it&#39;s duplicated please only delete the one in the inappropriate thread. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5221-->
<!--Post: 5248--><!--Time: 1106971835-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5248"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 8:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In these days of computers keeping track of everything, I&#39;m wondering if it isn&#39;t possible to track the cereal box by its bar code. If so maybe the lot #, which store it was purchased at, and the time and date of sale can be isolated by the itemized check-out list. This is assuming that BTK didn&#39;t cut out or otherwise delete any identifying info on the box, but surely he&#39;d be savvy enough to do that, and I&#39;m also sure that LE would explore this angle. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m curious as to whether it be possible to review in store surviellance videos for a time period in question in order to get a look at who purchased it? Maybe the store has cameras in the parking lot also, this could reveal a description of the make and model of car that the individual got into, and maybe even a liscence plate number. If he was on foot it still might suggest that he lives or parked nearby. <BR> <BR>Even if he was in disguise maybe the checker could recall something distinctive about him. <BR> <BR>Of course there is always the possibility that he has someone else do his shopping for him, but that still leads to potentially fruitful avenues of investigation. <BR> <BR>Or maybe he picked the box up dumpster diving or otherwise procured it through untraceable means, in which case the specific brand may hold no significance - beggars can&#39;t be choosers. But even this might suggest that he is adept at going unnoticed as an indigent person, and could be construed as bolstering one of my &#34;fantasies&#34;, i.e. that he is not an affluent individual. <BR> <BR>I like the idea of the brick/ paperweight as an obscure teaser. <BR> <BR>Anyway, certain individuals that frequent this forum may dismiss the aforementioned as the ravings of an opportunistic idiot - if so, sorry for treading your cyber-turf. And I certainly don&#39;t expect to be treated fairly or accorded legitamacy or acceptance through any form of socially interaction - which, in my mind, gives me a bit of insight into the rage and disdain that drives BTK. Hence my profile of BTK, on another thread.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5248-->
<!--Post: 5258--><!--Time: 1106983770-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5258"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Metalhead<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Metalhead<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->how about matching fingerprints on the box to grocery store employees and reviewing security tape??<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5258-->
<!--Post: 5263--><!--Time: 1106985438-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5263"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Metalhead, <BR> <BR>Good idea. I suspect he&#39;d wipe the box clean though. <BR> <BR>Also, I just read that from the Universal Product Code it is only possible to track an item back to its distributor, not the particular store that it was sold at - but maybe that&#39;s disinformation fed to the media by LE to keep BTK off his guard.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5263-->
<!--Post: 5328--><!--Time: 1107051081-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5328"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 6:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just how popular are Post Toasties in Kansas? I don&#39;t live there but where I live I was interested in seeing a Post Toasties box so during this week I shopped a little at each of the four major chain grocery stores in my area. None of them even carried Post Toasties. They had just about every other variety of post brand cereal available but no Toasties.  <BR>Maybe in even a big Wichita supermarket that carries Post Toasties they only sell a few boxes a week. As a cashier I would be wondering right now what customers buy Post Toasties. Then I would further think, do any 50-65 year old males come into my checkout line with Post Toasties? <BR>It&#39;s not one of more popular cereals. <BR>Then again as someone posted above it could have been retrieved from a dumpster and there would be no link to BTK or a wife of BTK ever purchasing them in the first place.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5328-->
<!--Post: 5335--><!--Time: 1107056236-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5335"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My hunch is the dumpster, too. If I wanted a cereal box within which to conceal incriminating evidence, I&#39;d get the box from a trash can. Better still, I might try a recycling center. This doesn&#39;t mean BTK didn&#39;t buy that exact box. As the books say, a BTK type gets complacent and you use his self-centeredness against him, as by this point I bet BTK almost fancies himself invincible.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5335-->
<!--Post: 5338--><!--Time: 1107057348-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5338"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 7:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think BTK killed those two other women murdered in that area..They&#39;re simply too old..I think he may have left the brick on top of the box as a confusion factor to make people think he did those murders when he really didn&#39;t...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5338-->
<!--Post: 5365--><!--Time: 1107066378-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5365"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dorothy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dorothy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 10:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It would be interesting to know if it&#39;s the same type brick used at Wichita State&#39;s Plaza of Heroines. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5365-->
