<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5388"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 8:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A bar code can be traced, unless it has been removed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5388-->
<!--Post: 5413--><!--Time: 1107111735-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5413"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 11:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There has already been an expert on KAKE saying the barcode is meaningless as far as tracing which store the box came from or who it was sold to...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5413-->
<!--Post: 5416--><!--Time: 1107113125-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5416"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Murco<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Murco<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 11:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->going with the &#34;post&#34; theme... he had to use POST TOASTIES, it would be too exhausting to sift through dumpsters looking for that brand. he probably picked up a box at a convenience store, paid cash, it is winter, so he could wear gloves etc. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5416-->
<!--Post: 5419--><!--Time: 1107113905-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5419"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 11:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->We are all assuming he cares about fingerprints at this point.  He did at one time.  Maybe he still does, maybe he doesn&#39;t.   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5419-->
<!--Post: 5441--><!--Time: 1107120839-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5441"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 1:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lubbock, good ideas about the box and bar code.  Even if the &#39;expert&#39; on TV is right and it does not pan out many companies keep such meticulous records that tracing an iten to at least a specific shipment or lot might well be possible.  This is just the kind of mistake that will trap him eventually. Some companies are even wanting to put tiny microchips in products which will be read at the checkout so they can do all kinds of automatic markeing research.  How many of such product was bought at which stores, time of day and day of week etc, even if they are paid for with cash.  I don&#39;t know if this is in operation yet, but there are lots of things citizens don&#39;t know. Big Brother does not care if we are honext citizens or serial killers, he watches us all.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5441-->
<!--Post: 5446--><!--Time: 1107123037-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5446"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 2:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->rfid tags...the chips printed with ink on the label...too soon I think to be of use...Walmart is testing a few pilots... <BR> <BR>The UPC should at least narrow down the range of possible stores...Then we know it came from one of those...It would narrow down the possible locations and number of clercks to interview...and who knows, maybe the discount card thing can still give us a possible list of names who bought PT&#39;s from those stores...long shots, but basic police work I am sure they are doing. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5446-->
<!--Post: 5448--><!--Time: 1107124804-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5448"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 2:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->POST TOASTIES...Post Toas Ties....Post Toes Ties...Any indication that any victims Toes &#40;feet&#41; were tied to a bed post?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5448-->
<!--Post: 5449--><!--Time: 1107125041-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5449"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Clairevoient<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Clairevoient<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 2:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Paper or plastic? <BR> <BR>58% solution <BR> <BR>The Post Toasties® were purchased some time ago, from a busy market outside of B_ _T_ _ _K®&#39;s immediate sphere.  <BR> <BR>You wore winter gloves while shopping and never touched the box with your cold icy hands.  <BR> <BR>You had a shopping list and purchased several other items. <BR> <BR>You wore a disguise -- plain but effective. <BR> <BR>You paid with cash, of course. <BR> <BR>You used a store coupon from the newspaper. <BR> <BR>You did something unusual with the receipt. <BR> <BR>&#43; <BR>Eyes open or closed - - why can&#39;t I stop seeing you… you blurry thing. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5449-->
<!--Post: 5538--><!--Time: 1107183046-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5538"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 6:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think it&#39;s as simple as this &#40;IMO&#41;... <BR> <BR>He needed a box with a nice big &#34;T&#34; on it so that he could sign it. But most importantly so it didn&#39;t draw too much attention. He wanted it to stay there untill he told the media where to find it. Notice the &#34;B&#34; and &#34;K&#34; could not be seen from a distance. <BR> <BR>The box could have been stove &#34;T&#34;op or &#34;T&#34;ampax. <BR>Sorry, just an example. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
