<!--Post: 5609--><!--Time: 1107217591-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5609"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 4:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Re: Post&#40;toasties&#41;  If he is indeed posting online, Maybe this was a message to someone, i.e.  watch what I post.Perhaps he has an ongoing dialogue with someone.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5609-->
<!--Post: 5617--><!--Time: 1107219267-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5617"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 4:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The trouble with the &#34;the brick has no meaning&#34; line of thought is that BTK left the brick in a location that is way outside his pattern, and is very close to several BTKesque unsolved crimes that are noteworthy for including the use of a brick. <BR> <BR>In other words, to believe the &#34;the brick has no meaning&#34; theory, you have to believe in a double-coincidence: 1&#41; BTK used a brick, which has significance, to weigh down the package, but didn&#39;t mean anything by it; 2&#41; BTK went outside his stamping grounds to leave the package in a location which has significance, but didn&#39;t mean anything by it. <BR> <BR>Is it possible that the brick means nothing? Absolutely! <BR> <BR>Is it possible that, just coincidentally, BTK used enough forethought to take along a heavy object to weigh down his communiques and the most convenient thing was a brick laying around in his back yard?  And furthermore that, just coincidentally, BTK was paranoid about police surveillance, so ventured along the periphery of his crimes to find a drop off location?  Absolutely! <BR> <BR>Should we require BTK to provide real evidence of involvement in crimes he&#39;d like to take credit for?  Absolutely! <BR> <BR>Is BTK be a liar and manipulator?  Absolutely! <BR> <BR>Does it seem noteworthy on a theoretical level that BTK left a package, weighed down with a brick, very close to the crime scenes of unsolved murders in which a brick was part of the m.o. and that are both outside his commonly accepted hunting grounds, and his historical clue-dumping grounds? <BR> <BR>Absolutely!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5617-->
<!--Post: 5913--><!--Time: 1107454371-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5913"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 10:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would like to comment regarding the circle that BTK traced on his box of cereal. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s not perfectly round and looks rather sloppy for a person who complained about a dirty car. It appears to me that he tried to correct his mistake by retracing it. Shaky hands maybe? At any rate, it&#39;s not what I would expect from a neat-freak, I don&#39;t think he is. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5913-->
