<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6549"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sjforcum<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sjforcum<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 9:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Has it been determined how long the package &amp; the brick were out there?  How was the weather for oh say a week prior to the drop?  Did it rain?   <BR> <BR>Based on the amount of paper visible &#40;paper box, paper streamers, etc&#41; that package couldn&#39;t have been out in the weather for very long...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
