<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6595"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 3:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Concerning drop #8 the return adress was  &#34;S Killett, 803 Edgemoor&#34; <BR> <BR>Found this researching on S Killett. <BR>Wonder if BTK is refering to this childrens figure as he refered to Kakeman? <BR>I know this is far fethed but BTK think in strange ways IMO. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.rhbnc.ac.uk/~uhle020/chegwith.html" target=_top>http://www.rhbnc.ac.uk/~uhle020/chegwith.html</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:K2SEtnKu6JIJ:www.rhbnc.ac.uk/~uhle020/a-gibson.html%2B%22Chegwith%2BSkillett%2BEscapes%22%2B&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:K2SEtnKu6JIJ:ww w.rhbnc.ac.uk/~uhle020/a-gibson.html&#43;%22Chegwith&#43;S killett&#43;Escapes%22&#43;&amp;hl=en</a> <BR> <BR>Chegwith Skillett Escapes  is posssibly my most lunatic book &#40;author Andrew Gibson &#41; <BR>Chegwith Skillett has escaped from a mental home, and just wants to escape the world and have done with it. The best way of doing this, according to Chegwith, is to find the balloon that his dead father - also called Chegwith Skillett - left behind him.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.rhbnc.ac.uk/~uhle020/bio.html" target=_top>http://www.rhbnc.ac.uk/~uhle020/bio.html</a> <BR>Andrew Gibson&#39;s Bio Page &#40;there is a person of the same name living in Wichita but that is NOT this author, wonder if BTK in som way has som dubble thing with names as he has with  dubble consonants?&#41; <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6595-->
