<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6619"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 5:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Chegwith Skillett. All I can say is that is interesting Skov. Especially Chegwith is pronounced with a S sound so one could forget the actual spelling of Chegwith and remember it as Shegwith thus S Skillett.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
